            {
                "entry_id": "d0528c95-fefa-35b0-939e-e6641b2693b1",
                "word": "tung",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e7beb62a-998a-4b62-b9be-e71b1149d438",
                        "entry_id": "d0528c95-fefa-35b0-939e-e6641b2693b1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tungs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                        "entry_id": "d0528c95-fefa-35b0-939e-e6641b2693b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete spelling of tongue, both as language and as part of the body."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd47d9da-cd97-450c-bea8-aa224ff68123",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "I am of this opinion that our own tung shold be written cleane and pure, unmixt and unmangeled with borowing of other tunges, …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27cf0a9e-ffa1-474a-8f00-93fb03659305",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "… ever exposed to their envy, and the tung of slander …"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5446c8e3-d9f0-4955-9994-f2db1d08d47f",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "Our common orthography is incorrect; the true spelling is tung."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5539c2d9-c092-466c-93ae-548f5408bfe6",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "… words to be spoken with the understanding, that I may teach others also, than myriads of words, in a tung. ... In the law, it hath been written, That, with other tungs and other lips I will speak to this people, and then they will not hear ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "255d2028-e49b-45f4-b5bb-1fd53894e91c",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "If they've got anything to say which they want you to hear, let 'em say it out; if not, hold their tungs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "df83a0a9-6418-48d9-90ea-3d25be07e21d",
                                "sense_id": "17389130-0aa4-39dc-8bb8-651cb1d1cdb5",
                                "text": "English has strength, simplicity, conciseness, capacity for taking words freely from other tungs, and best of all has the greatest literature the world has yet produced."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
